    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d71-a1">

                <pb facs="0132" n="82" sameAs="frus:frus1894/pg82"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No.
                    295.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Nascimento to Mr.
                            Thompson.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Minister for Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Rio
                                de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-09-22"><hi rendition="#italic">September 22,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>I have the honor to make known to Mr. Thomas L. Thompson, envoy extraordinary and
                    minister plenipotentiary of the United States of America, that the
                    vice-president of the Republic, by virtue of the stipulation in the customs
                    accord of January 31, 1891, has determined to denounce it and the proclamation.
                    This accord will continue to be executed in all its parts in Brazil until the
                    31st of December of the current year and will cease in all its parts on the 1st
                    of January, 1895.</p>
                <p>I improve, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Passiano do
                    Nascimento.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
